* ======================================================================
* coil_servo_parts.lib -- device models for the coil-servo power stage
* (Ansys Circuit / Nexxim syntax; used by ansys/build_project.py)
*
* Each .subckt is one purchased part (or one board). Where a number was
* MEASURED on our hardware it says so; DATASHEET values were typed from
* memory of the datasheets and must be checked against the PDF before
* they are trusted; ASSUMED values are guesses.
* Full table of sources: ansys/README.md
* ======================================================================


* ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* IXYS IXTN200N10L2 -- pass-bank MOSFET (linear mode), one of six.
* Channel law = the fit to our bench data (logs/t3q_offline/fit_bank.py,
* 5.18 V op-amp rail data, 11-11/12): smooth sub-threshold -> square law
*   I = K * [2 nUT ln(1 + exp((Vgs - VT) / (2 nUT)))]^2      (per FET)
* K 3.656 A/V^2, nUT 0.096 V, VT 3.892 V cold / 3.868 V warm (MEASURED,
* fitted, valid 0.05-2.5 A total; extrapolation to 100 A is NOT verified).
* The second (v(g,di)) term makes the same law work in the ohmic region
* and in reverse. Per-FET VT = fitted mean + (3 mA threshold - mean 3.525).
* CGS/CGD/CDS: DATASHEET-typical (Ciss 23 nF), constant -- the real
* capacitances grow several-fold below ~5 V drain voltage (ASSUMED flat).
* RLEG/LLEG: the 12 AWG drain leg, ASSUMED (length not recorded).
* ----------------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt IXTN200N10L2 d g s K=3.656 VT=3.892 NUT=0.096 CGS=22n CGD=1n CDS=2.5n RLEG=1.6m LLEG=150n
Lleg d dl LLEG
Rleg dl di RLEG
Gch di s cur='K*(pow(2*NUT*(max(((v(g,s)-VT)/(2*NUT)),0)+log(1+exp(-abs(((v(g,s)-VT)/(2*NUT)))))),2)-pow(2*NUT*(max(((v(g,di)-VT)/(2*NUT)),0)+log(1+exp(-abs(((v(g,di)-VT)/(2*NUT)))))),2))'
Cgs g s CGS
Cgd g di CGD
Cds di s CDS
Dbody s di DBODY_L2
Rleak di s 100Meg
.model DBODY_L2 d is=8n n=1 rs=3m bv=110 ibv=1m
.ends IXTN200N10L2


* ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* IXYS IXFN420N10T -- H-bridge switch, one of four (fully on or off).
* K chosen so R_DS(on) = 2.3 mOhm at 16 V gate drive (DATASHEET R_DS(on)).
* VT 3.52 V (MEASURED at 8 mA). Body diode: 0.5 V at 2 A (bench: drain
* bar sits ~0.5-0.9 V above the rail while freewheeling), 0.8 V at 100 A
* (repo model V_f), avalanche at 110 V (ASSUMED, 100 V part).
* Capacitances: DATASHEET-typical / ASSUMED, constant.
* ----------------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt IXFN420N10T d g s K=17.4 VT=3.52 NUT=0.05 CGS=45n CGD=2n CDS=12n
Gch d s cur='K*(pow(2*NUT*(max(((v(g,s)-VT)/(2*NUT)),0)+log(1+exp(-abs(((v(g,s)-VT)/(2*NUT)))))),2)-pow(2*NUT*(max(((v(g,d)-VT)/(2*NUT)),0)+log(1+exp(-abs(((v(g,d)-VT)/(2*NUT)))))),2))'
Cgs g s CGS
Cgd g d CGD
Cds d s CDS
Dbody s d DBODY_420
Rleak d s 100Meg
.model DBODY_420 d is=8n n=1 rs=2m bv=110 ibv=1m
.ends IXFN420N10T


* ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* TI UCC5350SB isolated gate driver (one per bridge switch).
* Output on only when IN+ high AND IN- low (IN- = DISABLE from the logic
* board). 3.3 V logic thresholds at 1.65 V. Propagation delay TPD 65 ns
* and output resistances RH/RL: DATASHEET-typical, from memory.
* GND1 (logic ground) is the global ground.
* ----------------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt UCC5350SB inp inn outh outl vcc2 vee2 TPD=65n RH=2.5 RL=0.6
Rinp inp 0 1Meg
Rinn inn 0 1Meg
Elog lg 0 vol='(0.5+0.5*tanh(10*(v(inp)-1.65)))*(0.5-0.5*tanh(10*(v(inn)-1.65)))'
Rd lg dl 1k
Cd dl 0 'TPD/690'
Eon on 0 vol='0.5+0.5*tanh(20*(v(dl)-0.5))'
Ron on 0 1Meg
Gh vcc2 outh cur='v(on)*v(vcc2,outh)/RH'
Gl outl vee2 cur='(1-v(on))*v(outl,vee2)/RL'
Rh outh vee2 10Meg
Rl outl vee2 10Meg
.ends UCC5350SB


* ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* Recom RO-0515S isolated 5 V -> 15 V DC/DC (one per driver), with its
* 1 uF || 10 uF output capacitors. Output 16 V unloaded (MEASURED: Q1
* gate 16 V when on). Output resistance ASSUMED.
* ----------------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt RO_0515S vin voutp voutn ROUT=15 COUT=11u
Rin vin 0 1k
Eiso x voutn vol='3.2*v(vin)'
Ro x voutp ROUT
Co voutp voutn COUT
.ends RO_0515S


* ======================================================================
* CELLS -- groups of parts drawn as ONE block on the schematic.
* Reason: Ansys Electronics Desktop STUDENT allows at most 50 components
* per circuit design; the power stage has 82. Every purchased part is
* still its own line below.
* ======================================================================

* One H-bridge switch position: MOSFET + its isolated driver + the
* driver's floating supply + gate resistors (10 ohm on, 4.7 ohm off,
* 10 kOhm gate-source). g = the MOSFET gate (for probing).
*   d, s   drain, source (the source is also the driver's floating 0 V)
*   inp    driver IN+ (polarity or its complement, from the logic board)
*   inn    driver IN- (DISABLE, from the logic board)
*   v5     +5 V logic supply feeding the RO-0515S
.subckt BRIDGE_SWITCH d g s inp inn v5
XQ d g s IXFN420N10T
XU inp inn oh ol vd s UCC5350SB
XP v5 vd s RO_0515S
Ron oh g 10
Roff ol g 4.7
Rgs g s 10k
.ends BRIDGE_SWITCH

* One pass-bank leg: MOSFET + 24.9 ohm gate resistor + 47 kOhm gate
* pull-down + Caddock MP930 0.030 ohm ballast. g, s = the MOSFET's own
* gate and source pins (for probing).
*   d      drain bar          gbus   op-amp output (common gate drive)
*   src    source bar (supply 0 V)
*   VT     this FET's fitted threshold (see IXTN200N10L2 above)
*   CGD    drain-gate ("Miller") capacitance, CGS gate-source capacitance
*   K      steepness of the current law, A/V^2 per FET (3.656 = the bench fit below 2.5 A)
.subckt PASS_LEG d gbus g s src VT=3.892 RG=24.9 RPD=47k RBAL=0.030 CGD=1n CGS=22n K=3.656
XM d g s IXTN200N10L2 VT=VT CGD=CGD CGS=CGS K=K
Rg gbus g RG
Rpd g s RPD
Rbal s src RBAL
.ends PASS_LEG


* ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* Littelfuse 5KP12CA bidirectional TVS across the pass bank.
* 1 mA at 13.6 V (V_BR >= 13.3 V), ~20 V at 250 A (DATASHEET clamp
* 19.9 V). Capacitance ASSUMED.
* ----------------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt TVS_5KP12CA a b CJ=8n
* smooth power law (solves more reliably than a hard diode knee):
* 1 mA at 13.6 V, ~250 A at 20 V
Gt a b cur='1e-3*(v(a,b)/13.6)*pow(abs(v(a,b))/13.6,31)'
Cj a b CJ
Rp a b 100Meg
.ends TVS_5KP12CA


* ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* EPCOS S20K20 (B72220S0200K101) varistor across the coil.
* 1 mA at 33 V, ~100 A at 80 V (DATASHEET) -> I = 1 mA (V/33)^13.
* Capacitance ASSUMED.
* ----------------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt VARISTOR_S20K20 a b CV=9n
Gv a b cur='1e-3*(v(a,b)/33)*pow(abs(v(a,b))/33,12)'
Cv a b CV
Rv a b 1G
.ends VARISTOR_S20K20


* ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* LEM LF 310-S current transducer. ip -> in is the primary conductor
* (positive current in at ip gives positive output current out of m).
* 2000:1. Response lag TAU 0.8 us (ASSUMED; datasheet: DC-100 kHz).
* Its +-15 V supply is not modelled (floating bench supply).
* ----------------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt LEM_LF310S ip in m KN=2000 TAU=0.8u
Vs ip in 0
Fx 0 x Vs 1
Rx x 0 1
Cx x 0 TAU
Gm 0 m cur='v(x)/KN'
Rm m 0 10Meg
.ends LEM_LF310S


* ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* Analog Devices AD8421 instrumentation amplifier, G = 1 (R_G open,
* MEASURED configuration), REF pin to ground. 10 MHz bandwidth at G = 1
* (DATASHEET-typical). Offsets and noise are not modelled.
* ----------------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt AD8421 inp inn ref out G=1 FBW=10e6
Rip inp 0 1G
Rin inn 0 1G
G1 0 x cur='G*v(inp,inn)'
R1 x 0 1
C1 x 0 '1/(6.2832*FBW)'
Eo out ref vol='v(x)'
.ends AD8421


* ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* TI OPA994 op-amp (gate stage). Gain-bandwidth 24 MHz, slew 30 V/us,
* output current limit 125 mA (DATASHEET-typical, from memory). The
* current limit matters: it is what makes the six gates (6 x 23 nF) fall
* from 4 V to 0 in ~4 us (MEASURED 11-12). Output reaches within 10 mV of
* its rails (MEASURED: 5.17-5.18 V on a 5.184 V rail).
* ----------------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt OPA994 inp inn out vcc vee GBW=24e6 SR=30e6 ILIM=0.125 ROUT=3
Rip inp 0 1G
Rin inn 0 1G
Gm 0 x cur='(SR*100p)*tanh((6.2832*GBW*100p)*v(inp,inn)/(SR*100p))'
Cc x 0 100p
Ra x 0 6.6Meg
Gcl x 0 cur='0.1*(max(v(x)-v(vcc)+0.01,0)-max(v(vee)+0.01-v(x),0))'
Go 0 out cur='ILIM*tanh((v(x)-v(out))/(ROUT*ILIM))'
Ro out 0 100Meg
Rs vcc vee 100k
.ends OPA994


* ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* Safety logic board (built 2026-11-03): 74HC04 inverter, CD74HC123
* monostable (220 kOhm / 100 nF, MEASURED 7.6 ms), 74HC74 latch with the
* reset button, 74HC10 NAND. Behavioural: the logic functions and the
* measured timing, not the chips' electrical detail.
*   dio0 = polarity, dio1 = bridge enable, dio6 = heartbeat (from E1)
*   rst  = reset button (high = pressed)
*   pol / npol -> driver IN+ of Q1,Q4 / Q2,Q3;  dis -> all four IN-
*   ok = monostable output (green LED), trip = latch (red LED)
* The latch POWERS UP TRIPPED and trips on the EDGE of the monostable
* dropping (as built) -- a reset pressed while the heartbeat is missing
* clears it and nothing trips it again.
* ----------------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt LOGIC_BOARD dio0 dio1 dio6 rst pol npol dis ok trip TMONO=7.6m
Rpd0 dio0 0 10k
Rpd1 dio1 0 10k
Rpd6 dio6 0 10k
Rpdr rst 0 10k
* 74HC04 #1: polarity and its complement
Epol pol 0 vol='3.3*(0.5+0.5*tanh(10*(v(dio0)-1.65)))'
Enpol npol 0 vol='3.3*(0.5-0.5*tanh(10*(v(dio0)-1.65)))'
* CD74HC123: retriggered by each rising heartbeat edge, times out TMONO later
Chp dio6 hp 1n
Rhp hp 0 1k
Gchg 0 c cur='0.05*max(v(hp)-1,0)*(1-v(c))'
Cc c 0 10n
Rc c 0 'TMONO/0.6931e-8'
Eok okn 0 vol='0.5+0.5*tanh(4000*(v(c)-0.5))'
Rokn okn 0 1Meg
Eokout ok 0 vol='3.3*v(okn)'
* 74HC74: s = 1 means tripped. Set by the falling edge of ok, cleared by rst.
Enok nok 0 vol='1-v(okn)'
Chp2 nok hp2 1n
Rhp2 hp2 0 100k
Vinit ini 0 PULSE(1 0 50n 10n 10n 1 2)
Rini ini 0 1k
Gs 0 s cur='1e-3*( (max(v(hp2)-0.2,0)*5+v(ini))*(1-v(s)) - (0.5+0.5*tanh(10*(v(rst)-1.65)))*v(s) + 0.2*(0.5+0.5*tanh(20*(v(s)-0.5))-v(s)) )'
Cs s 0 1n
Rs s 0 1G
Etrip trip 0 vol='3.3*(0.5+0.5*tanh(20*(v(s)-0.5)))'
* 74HC10: drivers enabled (dis low) only if dio1 AND ok AND not tripped
Edis dis 0 vol='3.3*(1-(0.5+0.5*tanh(10*(v(dio1)-1.65)))*v(okn)*(0.5-0.5*tanh(20*(v(s)-0.5))))'
.ends LOGIC_BOARD


* ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* Red Pitaya running the coil-servo firmware -- a CONTINUOUS-TIME stand-in
* for the fabric (the real thing is digital: 1.024 us ticks, 14-bit).
* The flip state machine, slew limiter and dither are NOT in here; the
* test sources on the schematic play their part. Verified firmware
* behaviour lives in the cocotb benches (sim/), not here.
*   in1  measured current   (IFSV amps per volt: 224 A / 1.12 V MEASURED)
*   in2  setpoint, same scale
*   pol  bridge polarity bit (DIO0): the loop works on current along it
*   run  > 0.5: servo running; low: OUT1 = 0 and integrator cleared
*   ol   open-loop OUT1 command in thousands of counts (0 = closed loop)
*   out1 behind 50 ohm: UVC volts per count into the 50 ohm terminator
*        (142.6 uV MEASURED), VOFF at code 0 (-41.3 mV MEASURED)
* PI: KP counts/A, KI counts/(A s); output and integrator bounded to
* FLOOR..CLAMP counts; zero-setpoint snap below SNAP amps; over-current
* trip at TRIP amps held for ~TTRIP (latched: OUT1 = 0 until the end).
* TLAT = loop latency (3.6 us, repo model).
* u (probe) = OUT1 command in thousands of counts, im = amps seen.
* ----------------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt RP_SERVO in1 in2 out1 pol run ol u im KP=31.2 KI=942e3 CLAMP=4100 FLOOR=3450 TRIP=2.8 TTRIP=4u SNAP=0.1 IFSV=200 UVC=142.6u VOFF=-41.3m TLAT=3.6u
Rin1 in1 0 1Meg
Rin2 in2 0 1Meg
Rpol pol 0 1Meg
Rrun run 0 1Meg
Rol ol 0 1Meg
Esg sg 0 vol='tanh(10*(v(pol)-1.65))'
Eim im 0 vol='IFSV*v(in1)*v(sg)'
Esp sp 0 vol='max(IFSV*v(in2)*v(sg),0)'
Rim im 0 1Meg
Rsp sp 0 1Meg
* over-current trip latch (tr -> 1)
Gtr 0 tr cur='(0.69e-9/TTRIP)*(max(0.5+0.5*tanh(2000*(abs(IFSV*v(in1))-TRIP)),0.5+0.5*tanh(20*(v(tr)-0.5)))-v(tr))'
Ctr tr 0 1n
Rtr tr 0 1G
* act: running and not tripped.  on: act and setpoint above the snap level
Eact act 0 vol='(0.5+0.5*tanh(20*(v(run)-0.5)))*(0.5-0.5*tanh(20*(v(tr)-0.5)))'
Eon on 0 vol='v(act)*(0.5+0.5*tanh(200*(v(sp)-SNAP)))'
Ract act 0 1Meg
Ronn on 0 1Meg
* integrator, in thousands of counts on a 1 uF capacitor
Gint 0 xk cur='v(on)*1e-9*KI*(v(sp)-v(im)) + (1-v(on))*10*(FLOOR/1000-v(xk)) + 10*(max(FLOOR/1000-v(xk),0)-max(v(xk)-CLAMP/1000,0))'
Cint xk 0 1u
Rint xk 0 1G
Eu uraw 0 vol='(0.5-0.5*tanh(400*(v(ol)-0.05)))*v(on)*min(max(KP*(v(sp)-v(im))/1000+v(xk),FLOOR/1000),CLAMP/1000) + (0.5+0.5*tanh(400*(v(ol)-0.05)))*v(act)*v(ol)'
* loop latency: matched delay line
Rds uraw da 50
Tdel da 0 db 0 Z0=50 TD=TLAT
Rdl db 0 50
Eu2 u 0 vol='2*v(db)'
Ru u 0 1Meg
* DAC behind its 50 ohm output
Edac dac 0 vol='2*(UVC*1000*v(u)+VOFF)'
Rout dac out1 50
.ends RP_SERVO


* ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* Bench power supply in constant-voltage / constant-current mode.
* VSET volts, current limit ILIM, sources current only. COUT = its output
* capacitance: 100 uF INFERRED from the 11-12 surge trace (not measured);
* RREG sets how stiffly it regulates (ASSUMED).
* For the Mean Well SE-600-5 use VSET 5, ILIM 110, COUT 10m (ASSUMED).
* ----------------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt DC_SUPPLY p n VSET=5.06 ILIM=3 COUT=100u RREG=20m ESR=30m
Greg n p cur='min(max((VSET-v(p,n))/RREG,0),ILIM)'
Co p c COUT
Resr c n ESR
Rb p n 10k
.ends DC_SUPPLY


* ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* Test fixture, not a real part: a connection that can be opened during
* a run (a pulled heartbeat wire, a loose BNC). ctl > 0.5 = connected.
* ----------------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt TEST_LINK a b ctl
Rctl ctl 0 1Meg
Glink a b cur='v(a,b)*(1e-9+(0.5+0.5*tanh(20*(v(ctl)-0.5)))*10)'
.ends TEST_LINK


* ======================================================================
* FAST TURN-OFF PARTS (docs/future_upgrades.md section 6). Planned, NOT
* fitted on the bench yet. Used only by coil_servo_fast_turnoff.aedt.
* ======================================================================

* ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* Littelfuse 5KP30A unidirectional TVS, rail bar (k, cathode) to return
* bar (a, anode). Stands off 30 V; breakdown 33.3-36.8 V at the test
* current (taken as 35 V at 5 mA); clamps 48.4 V at 103 A (10/1000 us
* pulse) -- DATASHEET, typed from memory: check against the PDF.
* Same smooth power law as the 5KP12CA: I = 5 mA (V/35)^31.
* Forward direction (return bar above rail bar) it is an ordinary diode,
* ~2 V at 100 A (ASSUMED). Capacitance ASSUMED.
* ----------------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt TVS_5KP30A k a CJ=5n
Gt k a cur='5e-3*pow(max(v(k,a),0)/35.0,31)'
Dfwd a k DTVS30F
Cj k a CJ
Rp k a 100Meg
.model DTVS30F d is=1n n=1.5 rs=10m
.ends TVS_5KP30A


* ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* IXYS DSS2X101-015A dual Schottky diode (2 x 100 A, 150 V, SOT-227),
* both halves in parallel, in the supply's + lead: a = supply side,
* k = rail bar. Lets supply current through, stops coil current from
* flowing back into the supply.
* Forward drop per half: 0.31 V at 1 A, 0.67 V at 50 A, 0.94 V at 100 A
* (DATASHEET-like: 0.77 V at 100 A hot, more when cold -- typed from
* memory, check against the PDF). So ~0.67 V and ~67 W at 100 A total.
* Capacitance and reverse leakage ASSUMED.
* ----------------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt SCHOTTKY_DSS2X101 a k CJ=1n RLEAK=200k
D1 a k DSCH101
D2 a k DSCH101
Cj a k '2*CJ'
Rl a k RLEAK
.model DSCH101 d is=20u n=1.1 rs=5m bv=170 ibv=1m
.ends SCHOTTKY_DSS2X101
